    "schemaxis.freecad.assembly/1": {
      "guide": "docs/freecad-assemblies.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Create an editable native fixed assembly with reusable constructor parts or verified typed PartDesign source histories, component links and named mounting frames. One source definition preserves its complete document; repeated components share its selected output Body.",
        "assumptions": "Millimetre geometry, one grounded component and a bounded fixed-joint tree. Constructor parts use box/cylinder definitions. Sourced parts use verified schemaxis.freecad/1 model.FCStd publications (workflow artifact index 2), including qualified multi-Body histories; the selected final output determines the instantiated Body. FreeCAD computes native placements; host frame composition supplies the independent oracle.",
        "constraints": "Fixed joints only: top/bottom faces for constructor parts, named mounts with parent-side offset and clocking for sourced parts; the two part forms never mix. Sourced assemblies refuse the optional GUI capture stage. No revolute motion, persistent assembly process, live editing or node inspection. Common analytic studies and scheduled workflow resume are supported. Timeout applies to each native stage separately for constructor parts and to the whole run for sourced parts.",
        "inspection": "Inspect saved components, joints, mounts, complete embedded histories and native perturb/solve/reopen evidence. Typed mechanical histories additionally require a configured FreeCAD launcher for fresh source recapture and regeneration: every indexed history element and actual subelement consumer must correspond, and all saved maps, shadows and geometry payloads must bind to that regeneration. Consistent object/StringID allocation changes do not excuse changed names, dependencies or operation spans. A rendered view alone is insufficient.",
        "recovery": "INVALID_GROUND requires an existing component ID. Repair joint endpoints or connectivity for structural errors. UNSUPPORTED_SOURCE names a source outside the qualified typed PartDesign publication contract; INPUT_CHANGED requires rebuilding changed producer/consumer runs. VERIFICATION_RUNTIME_REQUIRED needs a trusted configured FreeCAD launcher for typed history verification. Keep failed evidence; do not repair map or shadow failures by refreshing hashes or flattening history."
      },
