      "guide": "docs/freecad-analysis.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Construct and solve editable native linear static isotropic solid FEM from checked CAD geometry, with typed material, mesh, geometric supports and face forces/pressures.",
        "assumptions": "One homogeneous solid, small-displacement static elasticity, N/mm/MPa; straight-sided C3D4/C3D10 cells. Bundled FreeCAD1.1.x Gmsh and CalculiX2.23 are required.",
        "constraints": "Planar directional face selection must be unambiguous. Resource bounds, mesh/CAD volume tolerance and 2% face-area tolerance apply. No gravity, contact, nonlinear, shell/beam, multimaterial, thermal, modal or transient physics. Native cache equality alone is insufficient.",
        "inspection": "Inspect analysis.json, actual Mesh.inp/DAT/FRD and editable analysis.FCStd. Independent checks bind native mesh coordinates/connectivity, material, each nodal support/traction or pressure face, DAT/FRD/cache fields, force/moment equilibrium and strain-energy/external-work balance. Limits can be unmet while the calculation verifies.",
        "recovery": "Correct source units/facts, ambiguous faces and physically unstable supports; refine narrow walls/bores within resource bounds. Preserve failed evidence and use a fresh run directory. Rerun after material, support, load or geometry changes; editing a result cache does not solve the changed analysis."
