    "schemaxis.freecad.mechanism/1": {
      "guide": "docs/freecad-mechanisms.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Prescribe constant-speed angular or linear motion at named joints of a verified fixed assembly tree, retaining native Revolute/Slider joints, Simulation/Motion objects and a sampled mm/degrees/seconds trajectory.",
        "assumptions": "The initial assembly is grounded and fixed. Each motion starts at zero displacement and moves in its parent connector frame; offsets, clocking and serial parent motion compose. This is prescribed kinematics; it does not model loads, inertia, collisions or actuator feasibility.",
        "constraints": "One verified Schemaxis fixed-assembly publication or portable constructor packet; keep sourced producer run/provenance available. At most31 motions and240 intervals. Rotation is at most one revolution and15 degrees per interval. General closed loops, couplings, other joint types and arbitrary formula input remain unfinished. Each component remains a valid single solid. Both batch and private GUI runtimes are required; Xvfb/private D-Bus isolate native GUI settings and display.",
        "inspection": "Independent rigid-tree matrices, physical shape volume/solid count/centre of mass for every native frame, actual formula/type/joint/timing records, save/reopen and current-code regeneration. Verification never opens submitted mechanism files: it binds complete native object/dependency/property/GUI/payload state to trusted regeneration. Constructor source proxies are bound to a trusted native rebuild before opening. Native allocation IDs, UUID/create/save times and GUI payload filenames have explicit normalisation; referenced contents remain bound. Default constructor GUI root ranks are native owner IDs, bound under the object-ID bijection with explicit root order preserved; GUI-decorated constructors are regenerated with matching private GUI intent.",
        "recovery": "UNKNOWN_JOINT needs the source fixed-joint author ID. MOTION_RESOLUTION needs more intervals or less rotation. INVALID_MOTION needs a nonzero endpoint. UNSUPPORTED_SOURCE needs the complete matching producer packet; arbitrary FCStd files are refused. Retain failed logs and use a fresh directory after correcting intent. RUNNER_CANCELLED/RUNNER_TIMED_OUT retain incomplete evidence; do not treat partial frames as success."
      },
